# Project: World Front Page (g7-dashboard)

## Project Overview
- G7 + major economies (9 countries) news dashboard: top headlines in **Japanese / English**
- Host **titles only** — link out to original articles; no article body storage
- Single-page Next.js app on **Vercel**; data in **Vercel KV**
- Scheduled refresh via **Upstash QStash** → `POST /api/cron/fetch`
- Sister site: [Trend Dashboard](https://trends-dashboard.fly.dev/) (separate repo)

## Product Principles
- Fast scan: users grasp "today's world" in one screen
- Clarity over completeness; usefulness over feature count
- RSS / public feeds only — **no scraping**
- Treat external feeds as unreliable; handle partial failure gracefully
- Avoid feature creep; keep the product lightweight

## Tech Stack
- **Frontend**: Next.js 15 (App Router), React 19, Tailwind CSS, next-themes
- **Data**: Vercel KV (`@vercel/kv`), ISR `revalidate = 21600`
- **Fetch (prod)**: TypeScript `lib/fetch-news.ts` (RSS → DeepL → KV)
- **Fetch (backup/dev)**: Python `cron/main.py`, `npm run fetch:snapshot`
- **Scheduler**: Upstash QStash (JST 01/07/13/19)
- **Deploy**: Vercel (push to `main` auto-deploys)

## Architecture

```
QStash → POST /api/cron/fetch → lib/fetch-news.ts → KV (news:latest)
                                                          ↓
                                              app/page.tsx → Dashboard
```

| Layer | Path | Role |
|-------|------|------|
| Pages | `app/` | App Router, layout, metadata, sitemap/robots |
| API | `app/api/cron/fetch/`, `app/api/revalidate/` | QStash cron, legacy ISR revalidate |
| UI | `components/` | Dashboard, Header, CountryCard, Footer, modals |
| Core | `lib/` | fetch-news, news-sources, kv, types, notify-discord |
| Backup cron | `cron/` | Python RSS batch (GitHub Actions manual backup) |
| Docs | `docs/SPEC.md`, `docs/SCHEDULER.md` | Product and ops spec |

## UI / UX Rules
- Single page `/` — 9 country cards in a responsive grid (3 cols desktop, 1 col mobile)
- Bilingual UI via client `lang` state (`ja` / `en`); no URL-based i18n
- Light/dark via `next-themes`; explicit toggle, not system-only
- Prefer Tailwind utilities and existing CSS classes in `app/globals.css`
- Keep loading skeletons and `aria-live` for accessibility
- Practical UI tweaks over flashy redesigns

## News Pipeline Rules
- Source config lives in `lib/news-sources.ts` — keep TS and Python `cron/` in sync when adding/changing feeds
- Use **fallback RSS URLs** (`RSS_FALLBACKS`) when primary feeds fail (HTTP redirects, timeouts)
- DeepL translates titles only; respect rate limits and timeouts
- Discord notifications: **failure and partial fetch only** — skip full success (`lib/notify-discord.ts`)
- Log fetch outcomes; do not silently swallow country-level failures

## Coding Conventions
- TypeScript: `PascalCase` components, `camelCase` functions, `@/` path alias
- Python cron: `snake_case`, shared logic with `fetch_local.py` where possible
- Minimize diff scope; match existing patterns in touched files
- Comments explain *why* (feed quirks, redirect issues), not *what*
- Do not commit `.env.local`, `data/news-snapshot.json`, `.next/`, `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo`

## Error Handling
- Assume RSS feeds can fail, redirect, or return empty items
- Partial country success is acceptable; full cron failure throws and notifies Discord
- KV read failures on build: degrade gracefully (empty/mock path in dev)

## Security
- Never commit secrets; env vars via Vercel / `.env.local`
- QStash routes require signature verification (`QSTASH_*_SIGNING_KEY`)
- Check `git diff` before commit; run `./scripts/release.sh` before ship

## AI Development Rules
- Read `docs/SPEC.md` and `docs/SCHEDULER.md` before changing fetch or scheduler behavior
- When editing feeds, update both `lib/news-sources.ts` and `cron/main.py` if applicable
- Prefer small diffs; do not add heavy dependencies without justification
- Propose commit message in English; do not commit unless user asks or `/release --ship`

## Pre-Ship Checklist
- `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run build` pass
- No secrets in diff
- Discord/scheduler docs updated if notification or cron behavior changed
